{{Quote|Insert credit.|Comlink monitor|<ref name="Andor 2" />}}
'''Gavalox Communications''' was a [[subspace]] comm center<ref name="Trivia Guide">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e2-trivia-gallery|text="That Would Be Me" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor|quote=The business that Timm Karlo uses to tip off the Pre-Mor authorities about Cassian's presence is Gavalox Communications, a subspace comm center that promises "multi-network access" and "pay as you go" service that never closes.}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> on [[Rix Road]]<ref name="Rix" /> on the [[planet]] [[Ferrix]], that offered public [[comlink]] stations where people could insert [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] to use comlink booths.<ref name="Andor 2" /> The comm center offered "multi-network access" and "pay as you go" services that were available 24/7.<ref name="Trivia Guide" /> The sign on comm center stated the business' name in [[Aurebesh]] at the top and [[Bazeese script]] at the bottom.<ref name="Andor 2" /><ref name="GavaAurek">{{Twitter|AurekFonts|status/1574906951099908096|AurekFonts|date=2022-09-28|quote=Okay, gotta get real work done today too, but I wanted to start a dedicated Gingellbesh / Barrybesh / Barribesh / Bazabesh translation thread. This sign says: GAVALOX COMMUNICATIONS|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/isbJX}}<br />{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1574908242442043393|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-09-27|quote=I made this sign so people like yourself had a chance at translating it someday. I can't believe you are already across it.|archiveurl= https://archive.ph/f4myN}}</ref> The business name was also written in Bazeese on a street lamp, two lines of the same words wrapping around it, but with different [[color]] hues.<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>

The comm center was located close to [[Ferrix Depot]], [[Hotel Rix]], and a [[Unidentified chair store|store selling chairs]].<ref name="Rix" />

In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Andor 1" /> [[Timm Karlo]] went there to make an anonymous tip call about [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], who was wanted by the [[Pre-Mor Security Inspection team]] for questioning. Each booth contained a large comlink with various buttons and green monitor saying "INSERT CREDIT" in Aurebesh, with the credit symbol underneath. After Karlo pressed a series of buttons, the message "COM LINK D<small>''[obscured]''</small>T" appeared.<ref name="Andor 2" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The business that Timm Karlo uses to tip off the Pre-Mor authorities about Cassian's presence is Gavalox Communications, a subspace comm center that promises "multi-network access" and "pay as you go" service that never closes.|StarWars.com's Trivia Gallery for "That Would Be Me"|<ref name="Trivia Guide" />}}
Gavalox Communications was created for the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''. [[Barry Gingell]], who worked as a graphic designer on the series,<ref name="Andor 1">{{Andor|Kassa (episode)}}</ref> confirmed on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] that the script that runs underneath the [[Aurebesh]] name on the sign was a new alphabet created for the series, but he was not in a position to reveals its name.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|BazatronPrime|status/1574883352242429952|[[Barry Gingell]]|date=2022-09-22|quote=You are correct. It is the same new script. It does have a name. I'm just not sure I have permission to reveal it haha. That's a @pabl0hidalgo or @PhilSzostak level thing. Above my paygrade.|archivedate=20220928135536}}</ref> The name of the script was eventually revealed to be Bazeese script, in the episode guide for the episode "[[Rix Road (episode)|Rix Road]]."<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e12-trivia-gallery|text="Rix Road" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor|quote=The brick that Andor touches while sneaking around Ferrix is Clem Andor's funerary stone. It says, in Bazeese script: Clem Andor, and the dates 7896.39.5 - 7959.318.3. / The funerary stone that Brasso carries is Maarva's stone, and says on it, in Bazeese script: Maarva Andor and the dates 7895.330.9 - 7972.216.4.}} {{C|Slides 3 and 6}}</ref>

